meta {
  name: Search Users
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/search?q=test
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

vars:post-response {
  friendUserId: res.body.results[0].id
}

docs {
  Case-insensitive substring match on name, excluding yourself and anyone who
  has not set a name yet. At most 20 results, ordered by name. Expect 200 with
  { results: [...] }, each a public profile plus friendshipStatus ("none",
  "friends", "outgoingRequest" or "incomingRequest") and friendRequestId.

  Search for "test" to find the seeded test users. The post-response var
  captures the first result as {{friendUserId}} for the Friends requests.
  The seeded test users are already friends with each other, so use Create
  Test User and Update Profile to make someone new to send a request to.

  % and _ are matched literally, not as wildcards.
}
